notes:
  - mean_lnp/rank are measured on the entity's FIRST byte.
  - Δlnp vs 'prior OUTSIDE window (no memory)': positive means the model puts MORE probability on
    the entity's byte when it saw the entity before at that distance.
  - no-carry mode has no 'outside window' reference: long-distance buckets are
    the decay curve themselves (and 'cold' the no-memory extreme).
  - 'prior OUTSIDE window' is the de-facto >512 no-memory baseline for
    the architecture as trained (windows independent).
  - temperature must match training (T=1.3 checkpoint -> EVA_ALPHA_TEMP=1.3).
